@{ Layout="~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml"; ViewData["Title"]="Technician Help"; ViewData["RoleSubtitle"]="Technician Portal"; ViewData["UserGreeting"]="Technician help"; ViewData["UserInitials"]="LT"; }
@section Styles { <link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/technician.css" /> }
@section SidebarMenu { @await Html.PartialAsync("_TechnicianSidebar", "Help") }
<section class="tech-shell"><div class="page-toolbar"><div><div class="tech-eyebrow">Guidance</div><h2>Help &amp; frequently asked questions</h2><p>Quick answers for safe sample processing and result verification.</p></div><button class="tech-theme-toggle" data-tech-theme><i class="fas fa-moon"></i></button></div><div class="tech-help-grid"><details open><summary><i class="fas fa-box-open"></i> How do I receive a sample?</summary><p>Check the request number, patient, barcode and sample type. Select <strong>Receive sample</strong>. The receipt time and receiving technician are stored, and the request becomes Samples Received when all its samples are received.</p></details><details><summary><i class="fas fa-vial"></i> Why can I not start a test?</summary><p>The required sample must be received first, and the Laboratory Manager must have assigned that test type to you. A test can only be selected once.</p></details><details><summary><i class="fas fa-pills"></i> Where is patient context shown?</summary><p>When a test is in progress or returned for review, expand its patient-context panel to see clinical notes, active conditions, allergies, and current medications.</p></details><details><summary><i class="fas fa-check-double"></i> Can I verify my own result?</summary><p>No. A different technician who is authorised for the test type must verify it. Returned results include a review note and are sent back for correction.</p></details><details><summary><i class="fas fa-hourglass-half"></i> How are turnaround warnings calculated?</summary><p>The due time is calculated from the time the test was selected plus the configured turnaround time. The dashboard highlights overdue items and tests due within the next hour.</p></details><details><summary><i class="fas fa-file-pdf"></i> What is included in the report?</summary><p>The report is limited to your completed tests in the selected date range and groups them by category. It includes request number, urgency, completion time, and quality indicators.</p></details></div></section>
@section Scripts { <script src="~/js/technician-ui.js"></script> }


